{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7ec9eb6d-a417-436f-ba85-d0c2a218069f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0afa36396b1058c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-k3s_reif/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9002 (Integrated GenAI model evaluation for RHOAI)\n\nParent strategy: RHAISTRAT-9002 — Integrated GenAI model evaluation for RHOAI (Critical).\n\n## Triage\n\nNot below-threshold: the strategy spans five components (TrustyAI, Llama Stack,\nDashboard, Data Science Pipelines, Model Registry) owned by five distinct teams,\nwith HLRs from P0 to P2 and three explicitly flagged open questions. Not\ndocs-only: all affected components require code changes. Full decomposition\nfollows.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|\n| E001 | Evaluation execution engine investigation (LMEvalJob vs new service) | Investigation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P0 |\n| E002 | Evaluation result schema prototype (Model Registry custom properties) | Investigation | Model Registry | Model Registry | P0 |\n| E003 | Benchmark dataset licensing investigation | Investigation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P0 |\n| BRANCH-A-E004 | Extend TrustyAI LMEvalJob as the single evaluation execution path | Implementation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P0 |\n| BRANCH-B-E004 | Build a new platform evaluation service | Implementation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P0 |\n| E005 | Persist evaluation results linked to Model Registry model versions | Implementation | Model Registry | Model Registry | P0 |\n| E006 | Ship standard benchmark suites out of the box | Implementation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P0 |\n| E007 | Back Llama Stack's eval provider API with the platform evaluation service | Implementation | Llama Stack | RHOAI GenAI | P1 |\n| E008 | Dashboard views for evaluation runs and model comparison | Implementation | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| E009 | Evaluation step for Data Science Pipelines | Implementation | Data Science Pipelines | RHOAI Pipelines | P1 |\n| E010 | Custom evaluation task support | Implementation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P1 |\n| E011 | End-to-end product documentation for the evaluation workflow | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Documentation | RHOAI Documentation | P0 |\n\nMain-plan epics: E001–E003, E005–E011. E004 exists only as conditional branch\nepics (see Conditional Branches below), selected by the outcome of E001.\n\nPriorities: E001–E003 gate P0 work and therefore inherit P0. E011 is a\n`docs-authoring` epic exempt from priority inheritance; per the docs-authoring\npriority exception its priority derives from the strategy frontmatter\n(`priority: Critical`) → P0, even though HLR-9 is P2 (see Health Warnings).\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n  E001[\"E001 Investigation: execution engine\"]\n  E002[\"E002 Investigation: result schema\"]\n  E003[\"E003 Investigation: benchmark licensing\"]\n  BA[\"BRANCH-A-E004: extend LMEvalJob (branch A)\"]\n  BB[\"BRANCH-B-E004: new evaluation service (branch B)\"]\n  E005[\"E005 Persist results to Model Registry\"]\n  E006[\"E006 Standard benchmark suites\"]\n  E007[\"E007 Llama Stack eval provider\"]\n  E008[\"E008 Dashboard evaluation views\"]\n  E009[\"E009 Pipelines evaluation step\"]\n  E010[\"E010 Custom evaluation tasks\"]\n  E011[\"E011 Documentation\"]\n\n  E001 --> BA\n  E001 --> BB\n  E001 --> E005\n  E001 --> E006\n  E001 --> E007\n  E001 --> E008\n  E001 --> E009\n  E001 --> E010\n  E002 --> E005\n  E003 --> E006\n  E005 --> E008\n  E005 --> E011\n  E006 --> E011\n  E007 --> E011\n  E008 --> E011\n  E009 --> E011\n  E010 --> E011\n```\n\nArrows point from dependency to dependent (\"E001 --> E005\" = E001 must complete\nbefore E005 starts). Branch epics BA/BB are alternative instantiations of the\nE004 slot, not parallel work.\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → BRANCH-A-E004 | Rule 3 | Engine decision selects the branch; branch epic exists only under outcome A. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n| E001 → BRANCH-B-E004 | Rule 3 | Engine decision selects the branch; branch epic exists only under outcome B. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n| E001 → E005 | Rules 3, 13 | The chosen engine determines the interface evaluation results are captured from for persistence; approach changes with the outcome (`rewrite`). |\n| E001 → E006 | Rule 3 | Suite packaging and invocation are defined by the execution engine; scope changes with the outcome (`rewrite`). |\n| E001 → E007 | Rules 3, 12 | The Llama Stack eval provider adapter builds against the platform evaluation service, whose form is decided by the investigation (`rewrite`). Main-plan epic (exists under both outcomes), so it depends on the Investigation, not on a branch epic. |\n| E001 → E008 | Rules 3, 13 | The Dashboard surfaces run status via the engine-determined CR/API surface (`rewrite`). |\n| E001 → E009 | Rules 3, 12 | The pipeline step wraps the engine-determined evaluation launch interface (`rewrite`). |\n| E001 → E010 | Rules 3, 12 | Custom tasks run through the same execution flow chosen by the investigation (`rewrite`). |\n| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 | The canonical result schema is a true gate: persistence scope is rewritten around the prototyped schema (`rewrite`). |\n| E003 → E006 | Rule 3 | Licensing outcome rewrites suite delivery (bundled redistribution vs customer-fetch mechanism) (`rewrite`). |\n| E005 → E008 | Rule 13 | Side-by-side comparison of two model versions builds against persisted, version-linked results produced by the persistence work. |\n| E005 → E011 | Rule 11 | Docs are blocked by all Implementation epics; always last. |\n| E006 → E011 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n| E007 → E011 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n| E008 → E011 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n| E009 → E011 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n| E010 → E011 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n\nDeliberately absent edges:\n\n- No `konflux-onboarding` edges: every affected component is already Konflux\n  onboarded per architecture context, so no onboarding chain is generated\n  (Rules 19–20 do not fire — no new component enters the platform).\n- E007/E008/E009/E010 do **not** depend on the branch E004 epics: branch epics\n  are not main-plan nodes, and these epics exist under both outcomes. They\n  depend on the outcome of the Investigation (E001) instead.\n- E005 and E006 are parallel (different components/teams, no shared artifact).\n- E007, E008, E009, E010 are mutually parallel (different components/teams).\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Coverage |\n|-----|----------|---------|----------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004 | Evaluation launch against served models (KServe endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) — exactly one branch epic is instantiated. |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | E006 | Standard suites (MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag via lm-eval task names) out of the box. |\n| HLR-3 | P0 | E005 | Results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version. |\n| HLR-4 | P1 | E010 | Custom evaluation tasks (own datasets/metrics) through the same flow. |\n| HLR-5 | P1 | E008 | Dashboard runs/status/scores and side-by-side version comparison. |\n| HLR-6 | P1 | E009 | Evaluation as a Data Science Pipelines step for promotion gating. |\n| HLR-7 | P1 | E007 | Llama Stack eval provider API backed by the platform service. |\n| HLR-8 | P2 | BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004, E005 | Cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) is recorded by the execution capability and persisted with results. Bundled, not split: it shares the run-record data structure and persistence surface with the P0 work — splitting would duplicate the same schema (Step 4 priority-split test fails). |\n| HLR-9 | P2 | E011 | End-to-end product documentation including custom task authoring. |\n\nAll nine HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Open Question Disposition\n\n| Open question | Disposition | Rationale |\n|---------------|-------------|-----------|\n| 1. Execution engine (LMEvalJob vs new service) | Investigation epic E001 with conditional branches | The strategy explicitly requests a technical investigation with a recommendation; the answer changes which execution epic exists and what every integration epic builds against. Two bounded outcomes → branch epics for the E004 slot. |\n| 2. Result schema for Model Registry custom properties | Investigation epic E002 | Strategy requires a prototype against real MMLU output before committing; the answer rewrites the persistence epic (E005). Unbounded schema design → gate, no branches. |\n| 3. Benchmark dataset licensing / redistribution | Investigation epic E003 | The answer rewrites the out-of-the-box suite delivery epic (E006): bundled redistribution vs customer-fetch mechanism. |\n\n## Conditional Branches\n\nThe execution-engine investigation (E001) has exactly two bounded outcomes:\n\n- **Branch A** — build on TrustyAI's LMEvalJob (Tech Preview) as the single\n  execution path: `RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E004.md`.\n- **Branch B** — a new evaluation service that also serves Llama Stack's eval\n  provider API: `RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E004.md`.\n\nBoth branch files set `branch`, `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9002-E001`, include E001 in\n`dependencies`, and carry `gate_failure_impact`. No main-plan epic lists a\nbranch epic in its `dependencies`; epics that depend on the execution\ncapability depend on E001 (the Investigation) instead. Branch epics are\nexcluded from the main-plan critical path.\n\n## Component Mapping Notes\n\n- All strategy components map 1:1 to canonical names in\n  `.context/rhai-components.txt` (TrustyAI, Llama Stack, Dashboard, Data\n  Science Pipelines, Model Registry).\n- All five have architecture context files → all are in the platform; no\n  repo-onboarding / konflux-onboarding / license-validation chain is generated.\n- BRANCH-B-E004 (a new evaluation service) has no canonical component of its\n  own; it is filed under the closest parent-level component **TrustyAI** (the\n  platform's existing model-quality/evaluation component). If branch B is\n  selected, a component rename/registration may be requested at execution time.\n- Documentation is a canonical component but has no architecture context file;\n  it is a content (not code) component, handled as `docs-authoring` with no\n  provisioning chain.\n- **Model Registry is treated as active**, not passive: while custom properties\n  already exist as the extension point, the strategy's linkage requirement\n  (results tied to the *deployed* model version) builds on the registry's\n  role as source of truth linking model versions to serving deployments, so\n  E002/E005 are owned by the Model Registry team.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria,\n  no Non-Functional Requirements, no Technical Approach, and no Staff Engineer\n  Input. Teams were derived from architecture-context owning teams; the\n  Documentation epic's team (\"RHOAI Documentation\") is assumed since no owner\n  is stated anywhere. Acceptance criteria below are derived from HLRs.\n- **Docs priority inversion (rule-driven)**: HLR-9 is P2, but the docs-authoring\n  priority exception derives the epic's priority from the strategy-level\n  `priority: Critical` → P0. Flagged so a human can confirm this is intended.\n- **Scope trap — disconnected environments**: HLR-2 promises out-of-the-box\n  suites, but redistribution in disconnected environments is license-gated\n  (E003). If most suites turn out to be customer-fetch, HLR-2's \"out of the\n  box\" promise degrades; the E003 gate exists to surface this before\n  implementation.\n- **Tech Preview foundation**: Branch A builds on the LMEvalJob integration,\n  which is Tech 