mp does not invalidate or corrupt previously stored results.\n- The schema accommodates per-benchmark scores plus cost/duration metadata\n  (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time).\n- The report demonstrates how a stored result is resolved back to the evaluated\n  model version, including the served-endpoint-to-registered-version linkage.\n- The recommendation is concrete enough that the persistence implementation can\n  proceed without further schema design work.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Gates HLR-3 (P0): results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version\n  of the evaluated model.\n- Gates the persistence half of HLR-8 (P2): cost/duration metadata is part of\n  the schema under design.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38599,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a39b20e2ca4c4ad7","agent_id":"a3d693597663ee266","session_id":"811fcb9e-f25c-43e8-a4d0-4711eb32341e","uuid":"a15bbdd6-8af7-484d-a698-104ccaa6021f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:26:28.049Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
