{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-995ab0f4c6c4818c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n3\ttitle: Evaluation result schema prototype (Model Registry custom properties)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Evaluation result schema prototype (Model Registry custom properties)\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's second open question: what is the canonical evaluation\n30\tresult format persisted to Model Registry custom properties, and does it survive\n31\tbenchmark-suite version bumps? The strategy requires a prototype against real\n32\tMMLU output before committing to a schema. This investigation produces that\n33\tprototype and the recommended canonical schema.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Run real lm-evaluation-harness evaluations (starting with MMLU) and capture\n38\t  representative raw result output.\n39\t- Design a canonical result schema that fits Model Registry custom properties\n40\t  on ModelVersion entities (types and size constraints of the custom-properties\n41\t  extension point per the Model Registry REST API / OpenAPI spec).\n42\t- Validate that the schema represents per-benchmark scores, benchmark-suite\n43\t  versions, and evaluation run metadata (including cost/duration fields:\n44\t  tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) without breaking on benchmark-suite version\n45\t  bumps.\n46\t- Determine how an evaluation result is linked to the exact registered model\n47\t  version that was deployed and evaluated, using the registry's existing\n48\t  model-version-to-serving-deployment linkage.\n49\t- Deliver the prototyped schema, populated examples from real MMLU output, and\n50\t  a recommendation.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A prototype maps real MMLU evaluation output into Model Registry custom\n55\t  properties on a ModelVersion, retrievable via the Model Registry REST API.\n56\t- The proposed schema records the benchmark-suite identity and version, so a\n57\t  suite version bump does not invalidate or corrupt previously stored results.\n58\t- The schema accommodates per-benchmark scores plus cost/duration metadata\n59\t  (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time).\n60\t- The report demonstrates how a stored result is resolved back to the evaluated\n61\t  model version, including the served-endpoint-to-registered-version linkage.\n62\t- The recommendation is concrete enough that the persistence implementation can\n63\t  proceed without further schema design work.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- Gates HLR-3 (P0): results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version\n68\t  of the evaluated model.\n69\t- Gates the persistence half of HLR-8 (P2): cost/duration metadata is part of\n70\t  the schema under design.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb142f201910a446","agent_id":"a7feea8f854dd58c8","session_id":"811fcb9e-f25c-43e8-a4d0-4711eb32341e","uuid":"b9cec1cb-bafe-4999-b714-f38fe0ba0f59","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:40:16.527Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-995ab0f4c6c4818c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
