{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94656ed9641c620b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n3\ttitle: Benchmark dataset licensing investigation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Benchmark dataset licensing investigation\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's third open question: which standard benchmark suites can\n30\tbe redistributed by the platform in disconnected environments, and which must be\n31\tfetched by the customer? The answer determines the delivery mechanism for the\n32\tout-of-the-box benchmark suite capability.\n33\t\n34\t## Scope\n35\t\n36\t- Enumerate the candidate standard suites exposed through lm-eval task names\n37\t  (starting with MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag) and the datasets they load.\n38\t- For each suite/dataset, determine the license and its redistribution terms\n39\t  (redistributable in a product image vs must be fetched by the customer),\n40\t  citing the authoritative license text.\n41\t- Produce a categorized list: platform-redistributable vs customer-fetch, with\n42\t  license references.\n43\t- Identify the customer-fetch mechanism implications for disconnected\n44\t  environments (air-gapped clusters) for the non-redistributable suites, and\n45\t  recommend a delivery approach per category.\n46\t- Flag any suite where redistribution status is unclear and needs legal review.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Every candidate standard suite is listed with its dataset license(s) and a\n51\t  redistribution classification (redistributable / customer-fetch / needs legal\n52\t  review).\n53\t- Each classification cites the license text or terms it is based on.\n54\t- For customer-fetch suites, the report describes how a customer in a\n55\t  disconnected environment obtains and supplies the dataset.\n56\t- Any items requiring legal sign-off are explicitly flagged with the specific\n57\t  question legal must answer.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- Gates HLR-2 (P0): standard benchmark suites available out of the box — the\n62\t  licensing outcome decides whether \"out of the box\" means bundled\n63\t  redistribution or a guided fetch mechanism.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb142f201910a446","agent_id":"a7feea8f854dd58c8","session_id":"811fcb9e-f25c-43e8-a4d0-4711eb32341e","uuid":"73caa790-62c6-4d9c-be7e-71f3b2d7fdea","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:40:17.649Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-94656ed9641c620b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
