the served endpoint\n51\t  that was evaluated (KServe endpoint or Llama Stack distribution), using the\n52\t  registry's model-version-to-serving-deployment linkage.\n53\t- Persist cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) recorded by the\n54\t  evaluation execution capability.\n55\t- Read path: stored results are retrievable via the Model Registry REST API so\n56\t  downstream consumers (Dashboard comparison views, promotion-gating pipeline\n57\t  steps) can query them.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- After an evaluation run completes, its per-benchmark scores are retrievable\n62\t  from the Model Registry REST API as custom properties on the evaluated\n63\t  model's ModelVersion.\n64\t- The stored result is linked to the exact model version that was deployed and\n65\t  evaluated, resolved from the served endpoint.\n66\t- Stored results record the benchmark-suite identity and version and remain\n67\t  readable after a benchmark-suite version bump (validated per the schema\n68\t  prototype).\n69\t- Cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) is persisted with the\n70\t  result.\n71\t- Registry health: writing evaluation custom properties does not degrade\n72\t  Model Registry performance or existing registry UX (passive-component\n73\t  validation — the registry keeps working).\n74\t- Build pipeline green for affected repositories.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-3 (P0): evaluation results are persisted and linked to the Model\n79\t  Registry version of the evaluated model.\n80\t- HLR-8 (P2): cost/duration metadata persisted with results (persistence half).\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a64c0b42b7b2eae3","agent_id":"a960b39ae8f09b974","session_id":"811fcb9e-f25c-43e8-a4d0-4711eb32341e","uuid":"87192151-ab06-4dfd-806e-e9a838721639","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:57:46.741Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8b1c7ddeebe1857","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_typ