{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aef95a9bedfbca53","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n3\ttitle: Evaluation execution engine investigation (LMEvalJob vs new service)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Evaluation execution engine investigation (LMEvalJob vs new service)\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's first open question: should the platform build on\n30\tTrustyAI's LMEvalJob (Tech Preview, wrapping EleutherAI lm-evaluation-harness)\n31\tas the single evaluation execution path, or is a new evaluation service needed\n32\tthat can also serve Llama Stack's eval provider API? Produce a technical\n33\tinvestigation with a recommendation that determines the shape of all downstream\n34\texecution and integration work.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Analyze the LMEvalJob CRD and its job runner in trustyai-service-operator\n39\t  (upstream and midstream): current capabilities, extensibility, maturity gaps\n40\t  as a Tech Preview, and GA-readiness.\n41\t- Analyze Llama Stack's eval provider API surface (upstream meta-llama/llama-stack\n42\t  and the opendatahub-io distribution) and determine what a backing\n43\t  implementation must provide.\n44\t- Determine whether LMEvalJob can be extended to serve both the\n45\t  Dashboard-launched evaluation flow and the Llama Stack eval provider API, or\n46\t  whether a separate evaluation service is architecturally required.\n47\t- Evaluate implications for each option: KServe endpoint and Llama Stack\n48\t  distribution as evaluation targets, result emission interfaces, multi-tenant\n49\t  project scoping, and operational footprint.\n50\t- Deliver a written recommendation with the decision criteria and evidence,\n51\t  selecting between two bounded outcomes:\n52\t  - **Outcome A**: extend TrustyAI LMEvalJob as the single execution path.\n53\t  - **Outcome B**: build a new platform evaluation service.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The investigation report documents LMEvalJob's current capabilities and\n58\t  limitations as an execution engine for standard and custom lm-eval tasks,\n59\t  with evidence from the operator source and CRD definitions.\n60\t- The report documents the Llama Stack eval provider API contract and states\n61\t  explicitly whether LMEvalJob can back it directly, can be extended to back\n62\t  it, or cannot back it.\n63\t- A single recommendation (Outcome A or Outcome B) is made with decision\n64\t  criteria, covering impact on the execution flow, result persistence capture\n65\t  point, and the Llama Stack provider integration.\n66\t- The recommendation identifies which downstream work changes under the\n67\t  non-chosen outcome, so downstream plans can be adjusted without re-analysis.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- Gates HLR-1 (P0), and transitively HLR-2, HLR-3, HLR-4, HLR-5, HLR-6, HLR-7:\n72\t  the execution engine decision determines what the evaluation launch\n73\t  capability, suite delivery, result capture, Dashboard surface, pipeline step,\n74\t  custom task flow, and Llama Stack provider all build against.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2d0cf6b1f46f74d","agent_id":"a98001a3ef0046ed5","session_id":"811fcb9e-f25c-43e8-a4d0-4711eb32341e","uuid":"8019bd4a-1711-4d35-b72f-eb3cb1d3b613","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:02:00.605Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aef95a9bedfbca53","permission_decision":