{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac120f23aa5c2bcc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Extend TrustyAI LMEvalJob as the single evaluation execution path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine investigation does not recommend extending\n16\t    LMEvalJob, this epic is removed and the new evaluation service branch is instantiated\n17\t    instead.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Extend TrustyAI LMEvalJob as the single evaluation execution path\n35\t\n36\t*Conditional branch epic — instantiated only if the execution-engine\n37\tinvestigation recommends Outcome A (build on LMEvalJob).*\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tImplement the platform's evaluation execution capability by extending TrustyAI's\n42\texisting LMEvalJob integration (which wraps EleutherAI lm-evaluation-harness)\n43\tinto the single execution path: users can launch an evaluation of a model served\n44\ton the platform (KServe endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected\n45\tbenchmark suite, and the same path serves Llama Stack's eval provider API.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Extend the LMEvalJob CRD / job runner so an evaluation targets a served model\n50\t  (KServe InferenceService endpoint or LlamaStackDistribution endpoint), not\n51\t  only raw endpoints.\n52\t- Support launching an evaluation against a selected benchmark suite (standard\n53\t  lm-eval task names and, later, custom task definitions).\n54\t- Expose evaluation run lifecycle (launch, running, succeeded/failed) and\n55\t  per-benchmark results through an interface the Dashboard, Data Science\n56\t  Pipelines step, and Llama Stack eval provider can build against.\n57\t- Emit evaluation results (and cost/duration metadata: tokens, wall-clock, GPU\n58\t  time where available) at a well-defined capture point so they can be\n59\t  persisted against the evaluated model's registered version.\n60\t- Address Tech Preview gaps identified by the investigation for production use\n61\t  (error handling, project scoping, run limits).\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served via a KServe endpoint\n66\t  against a selected benchmark suite, and the run reaches a terminal status.\n67\t- A user can launch the same evaluation against a model served via a Llama\n68\t  Stack distribution.\n69\t- Evaluation run status and per-benchmark scores are observable through the\n70\t  exposed interface while and after the run executes.\n71\t- Each completed run records cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU\n72\t  time) alongside its scores.\n73\t- Results are emitted in the canonical result format recommended by the result\n74\t  schema prototype, at a documented capture point.\n75\t- Rollback/safety: extending the existing LMEvalJob path must not regress the\n76\t  current Tech Preview behavior (existing LMEvalJob usages keep working).\n77\t- Build pipeline green for trustyai-service-operator changes.\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- HLR-1 (P0): launch an evaluation of a served model against a selected\n82\t  benchmark suite.\n83\t- HLR-8 (P2): runs record cost/duration metadata (execution/recording half;\n84\t  persistence is covered by the Model Registry persistence work).\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2d0cf6b1f46f74d","agent_id":"a98001a3ef0046ed5","session_id":"811fcb9e-f25c-43e8-a4d0-4711eb32341e","uuid":"306d3f41-3ba6-49ce-87a7-c63d1679c7a0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:02:07.508Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac120f23aa5c2bcc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
