{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af66b32efce42132","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E004\n3\ttitle: Build a new platform evaluation service\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine investigation recommends building on\n16\t    LMEvalJob instead of a new service, this epic is removed and the LMEvalJob extension\n17\t    branch is instantiated instead.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: -1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 1\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Build a new platform evaluation service\n35\t\n36\t*Conditional branch epic — instantiated only if the execution-engine\n37\tinvestigation recommends Outcome B (a new evaluation service).*\n38\t\n39\t**Size note:** this branch is a functional envelope mirroring branch A. If the\n40\tinvestigation recommends outcome B with a large architecture, split this epic\n41\tat branch-instantiation time along its sub-deliverables (service core with\n42\texecution API and run lifecycle; Llama Stack provider adapter; per-project\n43\tdeployment) rather than instantiating it as a single epic.\n44\t\n45\t## Description\n46\t\n47\tImplement the platform's evaluation execution capability as a new evaluation\n48\tservice: users can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n49\tendpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite, and\n50\tthe service also backs Llama Stack's eval provider API so agents and apps built\n51\ton Llama Stack get the same results.\n52\t\n53\t## Scope\n54\t\n55\t- Design and implement the evaluation service (execution API, run lifecycle\n56\t  management, project-scoped multi-tenancy) per the architecture recommended by\n57\t  the execution-engine investigation.\n58\t- Execute evaluations by orchestrating lm-evaluation-harness runs against\n59\t  served models (KServe InferenceService endpoints and LlamaStackDistribution\n60\t  endpoints), supporting standard lm-eval task names and, later, custom task\n61\t  definitions.\n62\t- Expose run lifecycle (launch, running, succeeded/failed) and per-benchmark\n63\t  results through interfaces the Dashboard, Data Science Pipelines step, and\n64\t  Llama Stack eval provider build against.\n65\t- Implement the Llama Stack eval provider adapter surface so the service can\n66\t  serve as the distribution's eval provider.\n67\t- Emit evaluation results (and cost/duration metadata: tokens, wall-clock, GPU\n68\t  time where available) at a well-defined capture point so they can be persisted\n69\t  against the evaluated model's registered version.\n70\t\n71\t## Acceptance Criteria\n72\t\n73\t- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served via a KServe endpoint\n74\t  against a selected benchmark suite, and the run reaches a terminal status.\n75\t- A user can launch the same evaluation against a model served via a Llama\n76\t  Stack distribution.\n77\t- Evaluation run status and per-benchmark scores are observable through the\n78\t  exposed interface while and after the run executes.\n79\t- The service can act as the backing implementation for Llama Stack's eval\n80\t  provider API.\n81\t- Each completed run records cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU\n82\t  time) alongside its scores.\n83\t- Results are emitted in the canonical result format recommended by the result\n84\t  schema prototype, at a documented capture point.\n85\t- The new service is deployable per-project through the platform operator\n86\t  surface consistent with other RHOAI components.\n87\t- Build pipeline green for the new service's repository.\n88\t\n89\t## HLR Traceability\n90\t\n91\t- HLR-1 (P0): launch an evaluation of a served model against a selected\n92\t  benchmark suite.\n93\t- HLR-8 (P2): runs record cost/duration metadata (execution/recording half;\n94\t  persistence is covered by the Model Registry persistence work).\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2d0cf6b1f46f74d","agent_id":"a98001a3ef0046ed5","session_id":"811fcb9e-f25c-43e8-a4d0-4711eb32341e","uuid":"292b4dd5-74bd-4599-9e4b-165b51703288","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:02:08.910Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af66b32efce42132","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
