{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9404c43fa9b2caa0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E006\n3\ttitle: Ship standard benchmark suites out of the box\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If licensing rules out redistributing most suites, delivery shifts\n16\t    from bundled redistribution to a customer-fetch mechanism, rewriting this epic's\n17\t    scope.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Ship standard benchmark suites out of the box\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tMake standard benchmark suites (e.g. MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag exposed through\n40\tlm-eval task names) available out of the box, so users can select a known suite\n41\twhen launching an evaluation without assembling task definitions themselves.\n42\tThe delivery mechanism (bundled redistribution vs customer fetch) is determined\n43\tby the benchmark licensing investigation.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Curate the standard suite catalog: named suites mapped to lm-eval task\n48\t  names, selectable at evaluation launch.\n49\t- Implement the delivery mechanism per the licensing outcome:\n50\t  - For suites classified redistributable: bundle/distribute the suite with the\n51\t    platform so it works in disconnected environments without customer action.\n52\t  - For suites classified customer-fetch: provide the fetch/onboarding\n53\t    mechanism by which a customer supplies the dataset, including guidance for\n54\t    disconnected environments.\n55\t- Version the suite catalog so persisted results can reference the\n56\t  benchmark-suite version they were produced with.\n57\t- Surface the available suites through the evaluation execution capability's\n58\t  selection interface.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- A user launching an evaluation can select a standard suite (MMLU, ARC,\n63\t  HellaSwag at minimum) by name from the available suites.\n64\t- Suites classified as redistributable are available in a disconnected\n65\t  (air-gapped) environment without the customer fetching anything.\n66\t- Suites classified as customer-fetch have a documented, working mechanism for\n67\t  the customer to supply the dataset, usable in disconnected environments.\n68\t- Each suite carries a version, and evaluations record which suite version\n69\t  they ran.\n70\t- No suite is redistributed contrary to its dataset license (deliverables\n71\t  follow the licensing investigation's classifications; unclear items remain\n72\t  gated on legal sign-off).\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-2 (P0): standard benchmark suites available out of the box.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2d0cf6b1f46f74d","agent_id":"a98001a3ef0046ed5","session_id":"811fcb9e-f25c-43e8-a4d0-4711eb32341e","uuid":"62c8d70a-6820-46ad-819c-f5cc9555291a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:02:14.603Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9404c43fa9b2caa0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
