1\t  backed by the persisted, version-linked results in Model Registry.\n52\t- Launch entry point: initiate an evaluation of a served model against a\n53\t  selected benchmark suite from the Dashboard (form listing served models and\n54\t  available suites).\n55\t- Feature-flagged enablement via the Dashboard's standard per-component\n56\t  configuration mechanism.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Users can view evaluation runs for a project with live status and completed\n61\t  per-benchmark scores.\n62\t- Users can open an evaluation run and see its per-benchmark scores, the\n63\t  evaluated model version, and the benchmark-suite version.\n64\t- Users can select two model versions and see their evaluation results side by\n65\t  side for comparison.\n66\t- Users can launch an evaluation of a served model (KServe or Llama Stack\n67\t  distribution endpoint) against a selected suite from the Dashboard, and the\n68\t  run appears in the runs list.\n69\t- The evaluation views are behind a feature flag, off by default until the\n70\t  capability is enabled.\n71\t- The Dashboard continues to read component state through the Kubernetes API\n72\t  (no private component APIs introduced).\n73\t- Build pipeline green for the Dashboard repository.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-5 (P1): the Dashboard shows evaluation runs, their status, and\n78\t  per-benchmark scores, and allows side-by-side comparison of two model\n79\t  versions.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2d0cf6b1f46f74d","agent_id":"a98001a3ef0046ed5","session_id":"811fcb9e-f25c-43e8-a4d0-4711eb32341e","uuid":"eb345676-243a-4805-ae5b-e56634c6370b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:02:17.273Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84d1754ae1b93b6c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
