{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb85bc8c6683f87f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E010\n3\ttitle: Custom evaluation task support\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the engine decision changes how evaluation tasks are defined\n15\t    and executed, custom task support is rewritten for the chosen execution flow.\n16\tai_signals:\n17\t  change_specificity: 0\n18\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n19\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n20\t  existing_foundation: 1\n21\t  open_questions: 0\n22\t  external_dependency: 1\n23\t  human_process_gates: 1\n24\t  repo_access: 1\n25\t  architecture_claims: 0\n26\timplementation_type: null\n27\tinvestigation_signals: null\n28\tai_implementability: High\n29\tai_implementability_score: 5\n30\tjira_key: null\n31\tbranch: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Custom evaluation task support\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tLet users define custom evaluation tasks — their own datasets and metrics — and\n38\trun them through the same evaluation flow as standard suites, so the platform\n39\tanswers \"is this model good enough for my use case?\" for use-case-specific\n40\tcriteria, not only public benchmarks.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Define the custom evaluation task authoring format: user-supplied dataset\n45\t  reference and metric selection, compatible with lm-eval custom task\n46\t  semantics, consistent with the standard suite selection interface.\n47\t- Allow a custom task to be registered/selected at evaluation launch and\n48\t  executed by the evaluation execution capability like a standard suite.\n49\t- Include custom task results in the same persistence and comparison flows\n50\t  (per-task scores persisted against the evaluated model version).\n51\t- Validation and error handling for malformed tasks or unreachable datasets,\n52\t  with actionable messages.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A user can define a custom evaluation task (own dataset and metrics) and\n57\t  register it for use in evaluations.\n58\t- A custom task can be selected at evaluation launch for a served model and\n59\t  executes to a terminal status through the same flow as standard suites.\n60\t- Integration-level outcome (this epic implements the task format and\n61\t  execution, not persistence or result views): once the platform's\n62\t  result-persistence and dashboard capabilities are available, custom task\n63\t  results (per-metric scores) are persisted against the evaluated model's\n64\t  registered version and appear in the same result views/comparisons as\n65\t  standard suite results.\n66\t- Malformed custom tasks or inaccessible datasets produce clear validation\n67\t  errors without leaving orphaned runs.\n68\t- Build pipeline green for affected repositories.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-4 (P1): users can define custom evaluation tasks (own datasets and\n73\t  metrics) and run them through the same flow.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2d0cf6b1f46f74d","agent_id":"a98001a3ef0046ed5","session_id":"811fcb9e-f25c-43e8-a4d0-4711eb32341e","uuid":"ad67948f-26b9-4b4d-8e77-4f0e481d6005","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:02:22.985Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb85bc8c6683f87f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
